-- title:
--   Hyperbolic twisted classes parametrised by diagonal elements
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a finite Galois extension of fields and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (hypothesis `hgen`); $\sigma$ acts on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ entrywise through `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.map`. For $t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ write $I(t)$ for the set of $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ for which there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ with $t^{-1}\,(g^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(g))$ central in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, and write $H$ for the set of $\delta$ such that [`LT.TwistedNorm.normClassMap hgen`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L766) applied to the $\sigma$-conjugacy class of $\delta$ (the class of $\delta$ for the relation $\delta \mapsto g^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(g)$, sent to the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$-conjugacy class of a chosen norm representative of $\delta$ over $K$) equals the conjugacy class of some $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ whose characteristic polynomial factors as $(X-a)(X-b)$ with $a \neq b$ in $K$. Call $t$ diagonal if its $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries vanish. The conclusion is a conjunction of three assertions: (i) if $t$ is diagonal and $N_{L/K}(t_{00}/t_{11}) \neq 1$ then $I(t) \subseteq H$; (ii) every $\delta \in H$ lies in $I(t)$ for some diagonal $t$ with $N_{L/K}(t_{00}/t_{11}) \neq 1$; (iii) for all diagonal $t,t'$, the sets $I(t')$ and $I(t)$ meet if and only if they are equal, and they are equal if and only if there is $\zeta \in L^{\times}$ with either $N_{L/K}(t'_{00}) = N_{L/K}(\zeta)N_{L/K}(t_{00})$ and $N_{L/K}(t'_{11}) = N_{L/K}(\zeta)N_{L/K}(t_{11})$, or the same with the roles of $t_{00}$ and $t_{11}$ interchanged. In (iii) no condition on the norms of the diagonal ratios is imposed.
--
--   This is the parametrisation of the hyperbolic part of the twisted (base-change) setting for $\mathrm{GL}_2$: the set of elements whose twisted norm class is of hyperbolic type is exhibited as the disjoint union of the centre-saturated $\sigma$-conjugacy classes of diagonal elements of non-unit norm ratio, with the classes separated by the unordered pair of norms of the diagonal entries up to a common norm factor. It is used in the assembly of the hyperbolic contribution to the geometric side of the trace-formula comparison, and is cited by the lemmas that match hyperbolic terms across the comparison, such as [`AutomorphicForm.eq_of_norm_div_eq_norm_div_of_mem_of_disjoint_sigmaClasses`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.eq_of_norm_div_eq_norm_div_of_mem_of_disjoint_sigmaClasses).
